WEBVTT

00:00:00.023 --> 00:00:03.487
Our running project is a Student Support RAG Assistant.

00:00:03.487 --> 00:00:11.197
The knowledge base contains short documents about topics such as payment plans, internships,

00:00:11.197 --> 00:00:15.132
scholarship appeals, VPN troubleshooting, advising, registration, and graduation.

00:00:15.132 --> 00:00:23.112
A user can ask a natural-language question, and our system should retrieve the right source before generating

00:00:23.112 --> 00:00:30.452
an answer. For example, if someone asks what is required before internship registration,

00:00:30.452 --> 00:00:36.347
the system should find the internship checklist rather than guessing from general model knowledge.

00:00:36.347 --> 00:00:43.147
If the question is about VPN problems, the technology support document should move to the top.

00:00:43.147 --> 00:00:48.962
This dataset is small enough to inspect manually, which is useful for learning.

00:00:48.962 --> 00:00:56.387
At the same time, it contains the same kinds of metadata that matter in real projects: document IDs,

00:00:56.387 --> 00:00:59.202
topics, dates, sources, and permissions.

00:00:59.202 --> 00:01:05.712
We will keep returning to the same records so you can see exactly how data moves through a

00:01:05.712 --> 00:01:07.040
RAG pipeline.
